// The gauntlet harness twins' shared library. Metrics.jet names the
// loss-owner category of each metric, Tree.jet reads JSON values by path,
// Axis.jet holds what the axis adapters share (where one runs, the
// publication it reports, its contract rules and the probe of its tools,
// the twin of the tool-probe export of Tools/gauntlet/harness/run.mjs),
// CompileThroughput.jet is the twin of
// Tools/gauntlet/harness/compile-throughput.mjs (the compile_throughput axis
// contract and adapter), BuildSystem.jet that of the contract and adapter
// exports of Tools/gauntlet/harness/build-system.mjs, Coverage.jet the
// census library of Tools/gauntlet/harness/coverage.mjs,
// MemorySafetyFuzz.jet the twin of Tools/gauntlet/harness/memory-safety-fuzz.mjs
// (the memory_safety_fuzz axis adapter), Policy.jet that of the
// performance-law exports of Tools/gauntlet/harness/run.mjs (the strict
// performance policy, its issues, peers, metric applicability and ratio
// verdicts), Shape.jet that of its corpus-entry exports (loading the entries
// and the shape each must have), Result.jet that of its result-shape export
// (the shape a measured result must have), Comparison.jet that of its
// peer-comparison export (how Jet compares with each peer),
// Scoreboard.jet that of its scoreboard export (each matrix cell judged
// against its peers and its machine ceiling), Publication.jet that of its
// publication export (whether a run may be published, and what blocks it),
// and Probe.jet that of its HTTP probe exports (one probe of a service and
// whether its answer is the expected one). A program that uses it is a
// `<name>/run.jet` whose leading
// `package: { … }` block declares `jet_gauntlet_kit: <path to
// Tools/gauntlet/kit>` and imports the names it needs with
// `use jet_gauntlet_kit.[…]`.
name: "jet_gauntlet_kit"
version: "0.0.1"
edition: "2026"
